    {
      "id": 105,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Release lead time - commit to confirmed deployment (separate from the automated pipeline trace above)",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 50,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Release outcomes - PR creation through ArgoCD-confirmed sync",
      "description": "Each row is one release-outcome-span.yaml span (catalog/tasks/release-outcome-span.yaml) - a deliberately SEPARATE, standalone trace per release, not a child of the automated flow trace above. It exists because the automated pipeline trace intentionally ends at PR-open time (release.yaml's own end-flow finally task, gated on is-flow-terminal) - the PR's own human review/merge and ArgoCD's confirmed sync afterward are unbounded process time, not pipeline execution time, and appending them to the same trace would reproduce a real, already-fixed bug (a span reported after its trace's root already closed). 'Lead time' is the PR-created -> confirmed-deployed gap specifically, NOT total commit-to-deploy DORA lead time (which would also include the automated pipeline's own execution time, already fully visible as the 'stage:release' span's own duration in the Selected Flow panel above) - the two are deliberately non-overlapping. Outcome (Succeeded/Failed) is baked directly into the Release column's own text - Tempo's search API has no way to promote a matched span's status to a real flat column, only a per-row nested sub-frame Grafana can't render as a plain value, so the span's own name carries it instead. Correlate a row here back to its originating flow via chain-id (the same identifier the original flow's own spans carry as a `platform.chain_id` attribute) using Tempo directly - there's no reliable way to surface that as a dashboard column for the same nested-sub-frame reason.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 51,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "tempo",
        "uid": "tempo"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "queryType": "traceql",
          "query": "{ name =~ \"^release-outcome:.*\" }",
          "limit": 20
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "nested": true,
              "traceService": true
